on in the sky but  another dragon and that there is no need  to flee again as i mentioned in the last  review when this is animated this will  be such an epic moment with the figures  emerging from the cloud of dust as the  saviors of the country after all this  time people have already seen hiri  komorasaki who they thought was dead and  dendro aka boss kyoshiro these two were  part of wano during the 20-year time  skip but then kinemon one of the time  jumpers emerges to people's shock his  pose is amazing too i must say he really  makes the most of the reveal and they  comment on how they thought he was  burned in odin's castle some people even  think they may have passed to the next  life because this just seems like a  dream that's too good to be true then  oda is being pretty meta here hyping up  the moment by having a character say  real or not i think we're about to see  something monumental we obviously know  this as the readers but it's funny that  the people of wano are getting the same  vibes this is very much a payoff chapter  after the long long war and you bet ode  is going to build it up we see scabbard  after scabbard emerge we see what looks  like panda man to mark how monumental  this occasion is in the back between two  citizens we see kawamatsu inuarashi  hokage rizzo nekomamushi kiku notably no  ashrae doji though nevertheless people  proclaim it's the red scabbards who've  been assumed dead for 20 years  tokisama's prophecy did in fact come  true everyone's watching this broadcast  on their makeshift tvs in the different  regions including ringo hakumai and so  on to see what's happening so it's not  just a capital thing it's a nationwide  thing right here even udon is getting  the broadcast we then jump to some truly  epic game-changing stuff before the momo  face reveal it starts off as a hilarious  encounter between yamato and some straw  hats they're like what do you mean your  kaido son so this war isn't over but  yamato quickly points out she's not the  enemy she starts fangirling over them  saying she's been following their  exploits in the news for ages she knew  their crew was made up of a lot of weird  looking people but it's still a shock  meeting them in person and it's true we  got quite the diverse gang here but  yamato is different herself as they  point out she does have horns after all  not something you see all the time in  one piece it's hilarious how she just  announces the following and prepare  yourself she says anyway i'll be sailing  with you from now on i go by kozuki  yoden but you can call me yamato nice to  meet you end quote so this was the big  question all this time would yamato join  the straw hats we've been talking about  this as a community for a long time and  funny enough we also discussed this  exact topic in the newest episode of our  one piece podcast link in the  description animak was more sure she  joined than not and as i said i'd love  for that to happen but i didn't want to  get my hopes up after all her fruit is  literally the guardian deity of wano  fruit so you may imagine it's staying to  you know guardwano especially  considering momo is not a strong fighter  yet and it's not just me saying he's not  a strong fighter at that point we'll be  raised later on in the chapter as well  we'll get into this more later but for  now we see the crew reacting in their  unique ways to yamato's words nami and  usopp looking taken aback frankie  looking a bit skeptical and possibly  irritated of course brook and sanji are  acting like me brook says i approve and  sanji even says not as much as me robin  has a cool response saying haha how  amusing a bit characteristically cryptic  of her in that we don't know if she  means it's amusing to have her join or  it's amusing that she thinks she's going  to join and then jinbe with a very  professional response remarking we'll  need to get confirmation from the  captain before i'll be convinced and  yamato says fair enough now like jim bei  we can't be 100 sure what's gonna happen  yet but it looks good for us yamato  stands it's also interesting that she  wants the crew to call her yamato  meaning we still might get some odin  jokes here and there but she seems to be  developing more of a personal identity i  don't see luffy not wanting her to join  but again we need to see her take off  with them for my skeptical side to be  100 sure since as mentioned she is the  garden deity of wano and momo arguably  needs some more muscle if he wishes to  protect wano that being said this could  very well be the moment the tenth and  final member of the straw hats joined  the crew in retrospect and it would be  very satisfying after 1050 chapters to  have the 10 crewmates that luffy  mentioned he wanted all the way back in  chapter one i also think yamato would  make a great addition considering her  being unique as an oni princess a  mythical zone user a child of a  conquered yonko thus representing how  sun god luffy can overcome all barriers  her connection to ace her amazing power  that let her spar with kaido and so on  besides odin leader of wano went to  travel with roger and then came back so  why can't yamato travel and then come  back after they reach the one piece it  could work but let me know what you  think in the comments yes or no is she  the final straw hat let me know we then  jump back to luffy's current condition  chopper is doctoring him right now as  four kids would say they even mentioned  his new form and how that may have  affected him but nothing concrete as to  its consequences yet we get a funny  moment where yamato yells at some beast  pirates and jinbe concludes well this  one doesn't seem like an enemy at any  rate we then also learned that tama's  seemingly op powers do have a time limit  they wear off in a month and then the  victim can decide whether they want to  remain tame aka friends with tama or if  they want to leave there's some great  moments with horcella saying she wants  to stay and tama saying sure but not as  a servant rather more as a mother and  this just brings so much joy to hercela  nami and usop then see the broadcast and  how everyone is kneeling at the capitol  this is it it feels like momo's figure  is finally about to emerge from the  cloud he says it's been 20 years since  my father died he says everyone has done  exceptionally well to have survived this  protracted winter he goes on saying  they'll be able to go on living as they  wish after the festival they can drink  they can have free clean water the toxic  factories will be abolished slavery will  cease to exist wano has become another  place liberated by the warrior of  liberation aka joy boy sun god luffy  this speech makes tama think back to her  own flashback you gotta hand it to oda  he's definitely milking this reveal of  momo but it works and it's a great short  flashback of thomas we see that thomas  parents died working in a factory she  visited their graves and told them to  rest easy and she'll be okay we're shown  how she sold hats even though people  didn't have money to spare and hats are  not really an essential product even on  days she didn't sell a single one she  smiled and apologized to comachio it's  heartbreaking stuff but luckily we know  it'll turn out well then back to the  flashback we see our boy tanguyama being  kind and buying one of the hats he gave  tom a hope saying don't give in in a few  more years the kozuki clan's mighty  warriors will make their return and  wanna will be rid of those demonic oni  those words gave tama hope and renewed  her spirit and resolve one piece in  moments like this really shows how  important hope can be in life especially  when going through hard times and luffy  is so dangerous to the world government  precisely because he and his adventures  give hope to those oppressed by the  world government or other evil forces  thomas the orphan said she'll keep going  she'll be okay and she did and now in  the present kind of like hiri did  recently tama lets go she lets go  everything she was holding in the whole  time and cries in nami's arms she  recalls how a determined luffy told her  that by the time they leave this country  it'll be a place where she can eat as  much as she wants every single day and  boy did he deliver on that promise momo  goes on to say that orochi's tyrannical  regime and the menace of kaido are gone  for good i still don't think kaido's  dead but i agree that he'll probably not  be making any more trouble in wano as  we're shown a sleeping smiling luffy  momo remarks how he met powerful and  passionate friends on his voyage  together their ninja pirate mink samurai  alliance raided onigashima so boys at  this point it's definitely looking like  a successful raid i don't think we'll be  hearing any more about the raid failing  after this chapter this one arc really  appears to be over and what happens next  will probably just be leading into the  next arc momo says kaido orochi and the  beast pirates have all been vanquished  and vanquished just means defeated  thoroughly which we can all agree with  it's awesome seeing momo hold up the  sword in silhouette form it's such an  epic moment kid and law are pretty calm  compared to the ecstatic citizens  bawling their eyes out momo reminds us  that we'll never forget the heroes who  paved the way to make this possible and  then oda shows us carrot and toko who  lost pedro and yasu respectively they  are smiling knowing that their sacrifice  wasn't for nothing and helped bring  about this beautiful day we get a great  moment where momo acts like the  eight-year-old he is internally and asks  kinemon what he should say now as he  trembles kinemon smiles and says as they  say fake it till you make it a great  moment that's probably needed to temper  momo's sudden epicness he then screams  out that his name was given to him by  his father and it means second to none  he swears he'll 